Content follows the common telling of the Ramayana (Valmiki and popular tradition), much condensed: Dasharatha's four sons;
Shiva's bow at Janaka's court in Mithila; Kaikeyi's two boons; the 14-year exile; Bharata's rule with Rama's sandals on the
throne; Maricha as the golden deer; Ravana's abduction of Sita and Jatayu's fight; Sugriva and Hanuman; the ring, the burning
of Lanka; the Rama Setu (the stones marked with Rama's name are a popular tradition); Ravana's fall; the homecoming and
coronation. The link between the homecoming and Diwali is a popular tradition in many regions.
Everything else (score, foley, paper, all painting) is original and generated in code for this film.
Rendering and tools: the Lemo-Opuscar style library (Watercolor Brush style) and its core/ tools.
